P &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 2\\ \end{pmatrix} \\
Q &= \begin{pmatrix} 4 \end{pmatrix} + s \begin{pmatrix} 5 \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*} and \begin{align*}
P' &= \begin{pmatrix} 2 \end{pmatrix} + t \begin{pmatrix} 3 \end{pmatrix} \\
Q' &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \end{pmatrix} + s \begin{pmatrix} 2 \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*} be the given lines, we want these lines to not intersect.  Let $s$ and $t$ be real numbers so that
\[P = Q'\] and \[P' = Q.\]
